From 4ff470d3468bde3a81fab5f3d98ed2939c60dd15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taehyun Kim <dice.thkim@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 11:09:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/25] SCUMM: Harden the font map against untrusted input

Three problems found by review of the CJK generalisation:

The [bitmap] multi= value was handed to snprintf() as a format string,
so a map containing %s or %n made the call read arbitrary memory. Parse
the pattern ourselves and accept only a single zero padded integer
conversion.

get2byteCharPtr() only rejected negative glyph indices. A character
outside the code page's assigned range produced a positive index past
the end of the font buffer; bound it by the declared glyph count.

The coverage channel is a surface of its own, but writes to it were
bounds checked against the destination. Check it against its own size.

Also refuse to collect a run into anything but the text surface: the
flush happens a frame later, when a caller's own surface is long gone.
The caller now falls back to the per-character path instead.
